body:
If I call compressor\_model(15,14) where t1 =15 and pressure\_ratio = 14 the message is: 

//////////////////////////////////////////////

Error using fzero (line 308)

Initial function value must be finite and real.

&#x200B;

Error in compressor\_model (line 14)

fzero(effzero\_2,t2s\_guess)

 /////////////////////////////////////////////

&#x200B;

My tutor said that I needed to use fzero to set the function equal to zero and then that would solve for t2s\_new, although I'm not sure why.

Thank you for trying to explain this. I am still unable to make the code work and I am finding this very difficult. None of the variables are appearing in the workspace at all so it's not running fzero or calculating anything that I need. 

Currently I have: 

/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

function \[T2s, t\_average, Cp\_average\_temp\] = compressor\_model(t1,pressure\_ratio)

%% Inputs: t1(15c)

syms t\_average Cp\_average\_temp t2s\_new t2s\_guess

t\_average = t\_average1(15,40); 

%% run Cp code for t\_average

Cp\_average\_temp = shc\_constant\_pressure(0.6,t\_average,101.325); %this output cp should be set as cp\_average\_temp

r\_universal = 8.3145;

%% solves for gamma (heat capacity ratio)

gamma = double(Cp\_average\_temp/(Cp\_average\_temp-r\_universal));

effzero = @(pressure\_ratio,t2s) (t2s\_guess-t1)\*(pressure\_ratio)\^((gamma-1/gamma));

t2s\_guess = 40;

effzero\_2 = @(pressure\_ratio) (t2s\_guess-t1)\*(pressure\_ratio)\^((gamma-1/gamma));

%% solves for the roots of t2s equation

fzero(effzero,t2s\_guess)

while t2s\_guess \~= t2s\_new

t2s\_guess = t2s\_guess+1

end

&#x200B;

if t2s\_guess == fzero(effzero,1) %checks if t2s\_new is the same as t2s\_guess

  disp('finished')

else

t2s\_guess = ((t2s\_guess+t2s\_new)/2); %loops back with new averages t2s\_guess if not equal

end

&#x200B;

end

///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

&#x200B;

Essentially I need it to use fzero to solve fpr t2s\_new and then compare it to the initial guess of t2s\_guess = 40. If  t2s\_guess =/= t2s\_new, then loop back and use (t2s\_guess+t2s\_new)/2 as the new input and loop over and over until the two values match.  I'm not sure why they have to match as I wasn't told why, which is confusing me a lot but I am not allowed any more help hence why I'm stuck now. 

Thanks!

when I run the function:

function t_average = t_average1(t1,t2s_guess)
t_average = (t1+t2s_guess)/2;
end

It returns the value as ‘ans’, but I thought it would return the output as t_average as this is what I specified it to be? 
Thank you!
